  "_notes": {
    "units": "core/mem values are MHz offsets in the MSI Afterburner / Wattman convention (raw clock offset, not the 'effective' doubled rate). power is % of stock power limit.",
    "method": "Grouped by GPU architecture generation using real-world overclocking data from reviews, manufacturer OC guides, and community reports (2018-2026). Values are conservative daily-driver targets, not silicon-lottery maximums.",
    "laptop_note": "Laptop GPUs frequently have the power-limit slider locked at 100% by the OEM vBIOS/EC and cannot be raised in software without a BIOS mod. Power stays at 100% across all laptop tiers for this reason; headroom instead comes from core/mem offset only.",
    "caveat": "Within a generation, flagship dies (e.g. RTX 3090, RTX 4090, RX 7900 XTX) generally tolerate more power-limit increase than cut-down dies (e.g. RTX 3050, RX 7600) of the same architecture. These presets use a value safe across the whole family; higher-end cards in each group likely have extra headroom left on the table."
